# Proposed by the swarm (2026-10-14, from a day with real apps on a hosted Mac at macOS defaults); the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: an ordinary afternoon on a display of 1600 x 900. Finder is docked on the left, Safari on the right, and the
# Desktop between them is narrow, so Terminal, Notes, Mail and TextEdit are squeezed to stay on it. ⌃⌥⎋: Arbor lets go,
# and the Mac looks as it did before Arbor touched it: every window has its own size again, in view. ⌃⌥⎋ again, and
# the arrangement is back.
# Reference: F40, F48; "quitting, Float All and pause give windows back their own earlier sizes".
quiet
display-size 1600x900 31
open Finder 920x436
open Safari 1324x791
open Terminal 877x499
open Notes 1000x660 min 709x0
open Mail 1120x630 min 871x0
open TextEdit 673x439
move 101 340 120 920 436
move 102 138 31 1324 791
move 103 40 51 877 499
move 104 300 105 1000 660
move 105 240 72 1120 630
move 106 165 65 673 439

dock 101 left
dock 102 right
expect docked 101
expect docked 102
expect left-of 101 102
expect size 104 709x660
expect size 105 871x630

press toggle-pause
expect size 101 920x436
expect size 102 1324x791
expect size 103 877x499
expect size 104 1000x660
expect size 105 1120x630
expect size 106 673x439
expect visible 101
expect visible 102
expect visible 103
expect visible 104
expect visible 105
expect visible 106

press toggle-pause
expect docked 101
expect docked 102
expect left-of 101 102
expect camera root
expect size 104 709x660
expect size 105 871x630

# Framed on Safari, which fills the display, the same holds: Safari too is as it was. (Whoever only wants ⌃⌥ for the
# app in front has Shortcuts Off in "App", which moves nothing.)
zoom 102
expect fills 102
expect hidden 101
press toggle-pause
expect size 102 1324x791
expect size 101 920x436
expect visible 101
press toggle-pause
expect fills 102
expect hidden 101

# The keyboard goes elsewhere during the pause: a click on Finder, which the view that was left does not show. The resume
# ends with Finder in view, framed as Safari was, and ⌃⌥[ leads back to Safari.
press toggle-pause
focus 101
press toggle-pause
expect fills 101
expect focused 101
expect hidden 102
back
expect fills 102
